<title>USA: Colombia, eyeing US refineries, hires Smith Barney.</title>
<headline>Colombia, eyeing US refineries, hires Smith Barney.</headline>
<byline>Patricia Garip-Bertuol</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Colombian government, following the example of several other major state-run oil producers, is eyeing the possibility of securing U.S. refining capacity, Colombia's energy and mines minister said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In an interview with Reuters, Rodrigo Villamizar said the government has hired Smith Barney to evaluate the country's options, and expects the New York investment bank to submit a final report in March.</p>
</text>
